# A field read is a call on a reader the compiler writes for the field, and a
# literal the reader cannot take was refused in the reader's name: `[1 2].a`
# said no arm of `Get_a` takes a list. The runtime says a field is read from a
# record, and the check now says the same. Found on 2026-09-29.
type pt
  a

pub play = print "{[1 2].a}"
